title: 'Anthropic, "Effective harnesses for long-running agents" (2025): one part at a time, a list of parts marked passing only after an end-to-end test, and a record the next session reads first.'
pid: 612d6c7c-22a3-4524-9348-22bf1d8ccaa9
body: |2-
  https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-harnesses-for-long-running-agents
  Failures: trying to one-shot the whole, declaring the job done when
  it was not, leaving half-built undocumented state. Remedies: an
  initializer writes a list of features, all failing; each later
  session reads the progress file and Git log, checks the app still
  works, builds one feature, tests it as a user would, and only then
  marks it passing. Builders may change only the pass mark: removing
  or editing the tests is "unacceptable".
